 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# RLVR Reasoning Boundary Paradox — Full Training Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Hierarchical Capacity-Budgeted GRPO (H-CB-GRPO)**  \n",
    "> Investigating whether topic-level (macro) and prompt-level (micro) gating address *distinct* components of Pass@k boundary shrinkage in SLMs.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Research Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "| ID | Objective |\n",
    "|----|-----------|\n",
    "| **N1** | Boundary-shrinkage detection across 0.5B / 1.5B Qwen2.5-Instruct |\n",
    "| **N2** | Test whether existing mitigations (O-SELF, Static-SELF) transfer to SLMs |\n",
    "| **N3** | Capacity–shrinkage relationship analysis |\n",
    "| **N4** ⭐ | H-CB-GRPO: does macro×micro gating address *distinct* shrinkage components? |\n",
    "| **N5** | Interference diagnostics: does Δ⁺ mediate Gini → shrinkage slope? |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Notebook Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "| Section | Content |\n",
    "|---------|---------|\n",
    "| §0 | Install + Imports |\n",
    "| §1 | Kaggle/Drive mount + directory scaffold |\n",
    "| §2 | GPU verification |\n",
    "| §3 | **Module definitions** (all .py files inline) |\n",
    "| §4 | Self-tests (offline, no GPU needed) |\n",
    "| §5 | Experiment configuration |\n",
    "| §6 | **Exp 0** — Base model Pass@k + probing set + ceiling check |\n",
    "| §7 | **Exp 1** — Vanilla GRPO |\n",
    "| §8 | **Exp 2** — CB-GRPO (macro only, positive-mass refined) |\n",
    "| §9 | **Exp 3** — O-SELF (micro only, per-prompt solve-rate) |\n",
    "| §10 | **Exp 4** — H-CB-GRPO (CompositeGate = macro × micro) ⭐ |\n",
    "| §11 | Interference diagnostics (Req 40 / N5) |\n",
    "| §12 | Multi-seed delta-slope significance test (Req 42) |\n",
    "| §13 | Clustering basis ablation — difficulty-aware (Req 43) |\n",
    "| §14 | Cross-condition results + summary report |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Environment**: Kaggle (2×T4, 30GB VRAM total). Launch training cells via `accelerate launch` using the config in §3.  \n",
    "> **Resume**: All training loops are checkpoint-resumable from `run_state.json` — safe to stop and continue across sessions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
